 "title": "81 Loaves in the Oven",
 "sentences": [
  "In one Pompeii bakery, archaeologists found 81 loaves still in the oven.",
  "It's known as the bakery of Modestus, excavated in 1862.",
  "The oven door was shut, and the bread inside had turned to charcoal.",
  "Most were round loaves scored into wedges, easy to tear apart.",
  "Romans called this kind of bread panis quadratus.",
  "Someone put them in to bake, and never came back for them.",
  "Follow for more from Pompeii."
